  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a mechanistic link between vinblastine and SMMC-7721, mediated through a common target molecule, 3-[2-[4-[5-[2-(2,3-Dihydroxyphenyl)ethyl]-2-hydroxyphenoxy]phenyl]ethyl]benzene-1,2-diol. This compound is identified as the target of vinblastine and is also the target of multiple other entities, including MKN-7 and NUGC-3, which are implicated in the pathogenesis of SMMC-7721. The shared target suggests that vinblastine exerts its effects through a common pathway, likely by inhibiting the activity of this compound. The evidence is supported by a consistent score across different paths, indicating a robust relationship. The mechanism is further supported by the presence of a well-documented mode of action for vinblastine, which involves microtubule inhibition, a known pathway in cancer cell proliferation. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that vinblastine may act on SMMC-7721 through the inhibition of this target molecule, potentially offering a therapeutic strategy for this cancer type.",
